{"assets":["/statement-assets/40ea0f4deb1d2f3b01688f5c1b98dd0209c779b33f44b8d4faedeb0922c4b29f.png","/statement-assets/b8c0ea76f746084af0f848436bf49cd8232b496897a1f5b33df5eed95373ef4d.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"438","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. The Child and Sequence"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At the children's day, the child came to Picks's house, and messed his house up. Picks was angry at him. A lot of important things were lost, in particular the favorite sequence of Picks."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Fortunately, Picks remembers how to repair the sequence. Initially he should create an integer array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a[1], a[2], ..., a[n]"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then he should perform a sequence of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" operations. An operation can be one of the following:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Print operation "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l, r"},{"kind":"text","text":". Picks should write down the value of "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/40ea0f4deb1d2f3b01688f5c1b98dd0209c779b33f44b8d4faedeb0922c4b29f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Modulo operation "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l, r, x"},{"kind":"text","text":". Picks should perform assignment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a[i] = a[i] mod x"},{"kind":"text","text":" for each "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(l ≤ i ≤ r)"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Set operation "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k, x"},{"kind":"text","text":". Picks should set the value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a[k]"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" (in other words perform an assignment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a[k] = x"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Can you help Picks to perform the whole sequence of operations?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains two integer: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n, m"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n, m ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":". The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers, separated by space: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a[1], a[2], ..., a[n] (1 ≤ a[i] ≤ 109)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — initial value of array elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines begins with a number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"type"},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b8c0ea76f746084af0f848436bf49cd8232b496897a1f5b33df5eed95373ef4d.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"type = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", there will be two integers more in the line: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l, r (1 ≤ l ≤ r ≤ n)"},{"kind":"text","text":", which correspond the operation 1. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"type = 2"},{"kind":"text","text":", there will be three integers more in the line: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l, r, x (1 ≤ l ≤ r ≤ n; 1 ≤ x ≤ 109)"},{"kind":"text","text":", which correspond the operation 2. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"type = 3"},{"kind":"text","text":", there will be two integers more in the line: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k, x (1 ≤ k ≤ n; 1 ≤ x ≤ 109)"},{"kind":"text","text":", which correspond the operation 3. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each operation 1, please print a line containing the answer. Notice that the answer may exceed the 32-bit integer."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 5\n1 2 3 4 5\n2 3 5 4\n3 3 5\n1 2 5\n2 1 3 3\n1 1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10 10\n6 9 6 7 6 1 10 10 9 5\n1 3 9\n2 7 10 9\n2 5 10 8\n1 4 7\n3 3 7\n2 7 9 9\n1 2 4\n1 6 6\n1 5 9\n3 1 10\n"}],"kind":"s